## Security, Privacy, and Audit Requirements

- Enforce authorization on the backend; frontend route guards are not security controls.
- Scope all student, parent, fee, class, and academic-year operations to the authenticated school.
- Never trust a school ID or student/parent relationship supplied by an untrusted client.
- Test cross-school access denial.
- Protect student and guardian personal information. Do not expose sensitive fields unnecessarily or write them to logs.
- Audit important admin actions, including academic-year setup, promotion, student addition, exit/transfer, guardian linking, and fee collection.
- Use a new Flyway migration for any schema change. Do not rely on Hibernate schema updates in production.
- Do not commit secrets, generated files, or unrelated local changes.

